# Working with dude

[`dude`](https://github.com/cubocicloide/dude) is the project CLI — a single
entry point for all development tasks. Run `dude help` for a live overview, and
`dude help <command>` (or `dude help <group> <sub>`) for a command's flags.

---

## Installation

`dude` is published on the public npm registry. What you install
globally is the tiny **launcher** (`@cubocicloide/dude-launcher`); it then runs
each project's *pinned* CLI + stack automatically — no manual version switching.

```bash
# 1. Install the launcher globally (the only global install).
npm install -g @cubocicloide/dude-launcher
```

Then, inside this project, provision the pinned toolchain (the launcher would
also do this on the first `dude` command, but doing it explicitly is clearer):

```bash
pnpm install      # installs the pinned @cubocicloide/dude CLI + stack
dude version      # verify the resolved CLI + stack versions
```


---

## Getting started

### First run

```bash
dude up
dude logs --service bench   # follow the provisioning
```

The **first** boot does real work — `docker/init.sh` creates the bench
(downloads Frappe v15), creates the site{{#if withHelpdesk}}, installs Frappe
Helpdesk{{/if}}, installs every custom app under `apps/`, and runs
`bench migrate` — expect several minutes. Every later `dude up` reuses the
provisioned bench (persisted in the `bench_home` volume) and is fast. The
script is idempotent, so restarting mid-provision is safe.

### Services

Once `bench start` is running:

| Service | URL | Notes |
|---------|-----|-------|
| **Desk** | http://{{projectName}}.localhost:8000/app | Admin UI — `Administrator` / `admin` |
{{#if withHelpdesk}}| **Helpdesk** | http://{{projectName}}.localhost:8000/helpdesk | Agent UI (Frappe Helpdesk) |
{{/if}}| **Portal example** | http://{{projectName}}.localhost:8000/ticket_stats | Public page from `apps/ticketing` |
| **API example** | http://{{projectName}}.localhost:8000/api/method/ticketing.api.ticket_stats | Whitelisted method |

### Hot reload

`apps/` is mounted into the container and installed in **editable mode**: edit
Python under `apps/ticketing/` on the host and the dev server reloads within a
second or two. Changes to a DocType **schema** (`.json`) or to fixtures need
`dude site migrate`; changes to `hooks.py` need a restart (`dude up`).

