## Infrastructure

All services run in Docker. The `docker-compose.yml` at the project root
defines every service (`mariadb`, `redis-cache`, `redis-queue`, `bench`).

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `dude up` | Start all services (detached) |
| `dude up --build` | Rebuild images first |
| `dude down` | Stop and remove containers (bench + DB volumes survive) |
| `dude down --volumes` | Also remove volumes — **destroys the bench and the database** |
| `dude logs` | Follow logs for all services |
| `dude logs --service bench` | Follow logs for one service |
| `dude shell` | Interactive shell in the bench container, inside `frappe-bench/` |
| `dude shell --service mariadb` | Shell into another service |

---

## Bench passthrough

`bench` is Frappe's own CLI. Anything `dude` doesn't wrap explicitly is one
passthrough away — everything after `dude bench` runs verbatim as `bench …`
inside the bench container:

```bash
dude bench --site all migrate
dude bench --site all execute ticketing.tasks.escalate_overdue_tickets
dude bench --site all export-fixtures --app ticketing
dude bench version
```

---

## Site operations

Day-to-day operations on the default site (`SITE_NAME` from `.env`):

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `dude site migrate` | Apply pending schema changes, patches and fixtures (`bench migrate`) |
| `dude site console` | IPython console with the site loaded — try `frappe.get_all("Ticket Escalation Rule")` |
| `dude site backup` | Backup the database → `sites/<site>/private/backups` |
| `dude site backup --files` | Also include public/private files |
| `dude site clear-cache` | Clear the site + website cache |
| `dude site mariadb` | SQL client connected to the site's database |

Run `dude site migrate` after: adding/editing a DocType JSON, changing
fixtures, or pulling schema changes from git. (It also runs automatically on
every container boot.)

