## Documentation

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `dude docs` | Serve this documentation in dev mode at <http://localhost:8001> |
| `dude docs --port 9000` | Use a custom port |
| `dude help --format md` | Print the full command reference as Markdown |
| `dude help --format json` | Print the same catalog as JSON (for tooling / LLMs) |

The **Command reference** page in this site is auto-generated from the live
command catalog every time you run `dude docs`, so it always matches your
project's actual commands — including your `dude init` choices and any
project-local commands under `.dude/commands/`. (It is gitignored; regenerate it
any time with `dude docs` or `dude help --format md`.)

The docs site live-reloads when you edit files under `docs/docs/`.

```bash
dude docs
# → open http://localhost:8001
# → edit docs/docs/*.md
# → browser refreshes automatically
```
